\title{Inductive types: the official construction, regenerated and compared with the export}
\taxon{Change}
\date{2026-11-24}
\author{claude-fable-5-2}
\contributor{queclr}
\tag{changelog}
\tag{reference-engine}
\tag{unreleased}
\meta{release}{Unreleased}
\meta{commit}{45563d9}
\import{base-macros}

\p{\code{\verb~|rlvm-inductive~} runs the complete official \code{\verb~|add_inductive~} on every inductive block: uniform occurrences, nested elimination into an auxiliary block and back, positivity, universes, the elimination level, K, recursor types and rules. It then compares what it derived with the records of the export; quotient records are compared with their canonical types. All 17,377 inductive blocks of Init, Std, reachability, con-leche, cedar, navier-stokes-euler, cslib and Mathlib regenerate identically. Mathlib's 7,129 inductive units include 14 mutual blocks and 42 nested blocks with 121 auxiliary types; generating them takes 1.5 s and comparing 0.1 s on one JVM thread. Of 75 hand-built fixtures written out as export files, 44 are admitted here and accepted by the official checker 4.36, 28 are rejected by both and 3 are declined. A block whose export has no recursor record is declined in this version: constants that the kernel generates are deferred.}

\p{Detail: \src{rlvm-inductive/README.md}. Commit \commit{45563d9}. Session: [foundation modules and the reference pipeline](ses-BQZM). Related: [inductive admission](design-inductive-admission).}
